    {
      "id": "PP36QVwUkCOdJpQ1Dboy1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3379.802635290588,
      "y": -610.3455085214441,
      "width": 796.14306640625,
      "height": 2380,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 70,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2014130038,
      "version": 2684,
      "versionNonce": 164848758,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1746555297459,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design Red Bus/ Bus Booking system . ( Db schema, HLD)\n\n\nFunctional Requirements: \n1.  we have bus -> list of seats\n2. user book the sheats , user can be concurrent.\n3. partial booking ?? -> not allow \n4. flow -> user select the seats -> user do the payment\n   what behaviour to to user -> irctc kind of block, red bus kind of\n   blur for few min and revert if payment fails. -> other user\n   will see the booked seat if someone doing payment for some \n   time \n5. how payment we wanna discuss how much we \n   want to store on our side ??  what's the flow of payment\n   in booking. \n\n\nNFR: \n1.  scalabilty\n2. consistency -> no double booking. \n3. consistency > avaliabitliy -> can possible seat unavailable\nfor other customer than booking wrong. \n4. alerts and monitoring. \n5. idempotency.\n\n\nEstimations:  -> later on on this. \n1. booking requests -> peak qps. \n2. assume -> high concurrent requests.\n\n\n\nEntity:\nuser , bus, seat, booking, payment order \n\nApi Design: \n\n1. get the bus seat arrangement. \n2. book the seat \n\n/api/v1/booking/book        POST https: \n\nx-token -> sessionId -> idempotent kay for double click.\n\nRequest: {\nrequestMeta: {\n    app: \"\"\n    globalContextId: \"\"\n  }\n  busTravelId: <>, \n  seats: [<1>, <2>],\n}\n\nResponse: {\n  status Code -> 200 \n  bookingId: <>\n}\n\n\n3. /api/v1/booking/webhook/payment POST\n\nRequest: {\n   bookingId.        -> idempotent key for payment system\n   status: \n   authDetails: \n}\n\n\n\n\nDb schema: \n\n1. User\n    - id\n    - email\n    .... \n    \n2. Bus\n    - id PK\n    - name\n    - owner\n    - ...\n\n3. BusTravel\n    - busid\n    - id PK\n    - date\n    - starttime\n    - endtime\n    - source\n    - destnation\n    - total seats\n    ... \n4. BusTravelSeat\n    - BusTravelid\n    - seatId\n    - status -> / available | unavailalble\n\n5. Booking\n    - seats: [seatid1, seatid2]. or booking seat modell\n    - bustravelId\n    - bookedBy\n    - createdTime\n    - updatedTime\n    - status -> PENDING, COMPLETED, FAILED\n    - timeOut -> at which time it would fail if not completed , at this time all seats will be un available\n    - bookingId\n    - amount\n    - usersessionId\n\n6. PaymentOrder\n    - id\n    - bookingId\n    - amount\n    - status\n    \n\n\nHigh Level Design",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design Red Bus/ Bus Booking system . ( Db schema, HLD)\n\n\nFunctional Requirements: \n1.  we have bus -> list of seats\n2. user book the sheats , user can be concurrent.\n3. partial booking ?? -> not allow \n4. flow -> user select the seats -> user do the payment\n   what behaviour to to user -> irctc kind of block, red bus kind of\n   blur for few min and revert if payment fails. -> other user\n   will see the booked seat if someone doing payment for some \n   time \n5. how payment we wanna discuss how much we \n   want to store on our side ??  what's the flow of payment\n   in booking. \n\n\nNFR: \n1.  scalabilty\n2. consistency -> no double booking. \n3. consistency > avaliabitliy -> can possible seat unavailable\nfor other customer than booking wrong. \n4. alerts and monitoring. \n5. idempotency.\n\n\nEstimations:  -> later on on this. \n1. booking requests -> peak qps. \n2. assume -> high concurrent requests.\n\n\n\nEntity:\nuser , bus, seat, booking, payment order \n\nApi Design: \n\n1. get the bus seat arrangement. \n2. book the seat \n\n/api/v1/booking/book        POST https: \n\nx-token -> sessionId -> idempotent kay for double click.\n\nRequest: {\nrequestMeta: {\n    app: \"\"\n    globalContextId: \"\"\n  }\n  busTravelId: <>, \n  seats: [<1>, <2>],\n}\n\nResponse: {\n  status Code -> 200 \n  bookingId: <>\n}\n\n\n3. /api/v1/booking/webhook/payment POST\n\nRequest: {\n   bookingId.        -> idempotent key for payment system\n   status: \n   authDetails: \n}\n\n\n\n\nDb schema: \n\n1. User\n    - id\n    - email\n    .... \n    \n2. Bus\n    - id PK\n    - name\n    - owner\n    - ...\n\n3. BusTravel\n    - busid\n    - id PK\n    - date\n    - starttime\n    - endtime\n    - source\n    - destnation\n    - total seats\n    ... \n4. BusTravelSeat\n    - BusTravelid\n    - seatId\n    - status -> / available | unavailalble\n\n5. Booking\n    - seats: [seatid1, seatid2]. or booking seat modell\n    - bustravelId\n    - bookedBy\n    - createdTime\n    - updatedTime\n    - status -> PENDING, COMPLETED, FAILED\n    - timeOut -> at which time it would fail if not completed , at this time all seats will be un available\n    - bookingId\n    - amount\n    - usersessionId\n\n6. PaymentOrder\n    - id\n    - bookingId\n    - amount\n    - status\n    \n\n\nHigh Level Design",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
