      "locked": false,
      "text": "restriction\nto go inside",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "restriction\nto go inside",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Y_953KrK0YtHZfc8CSebS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6242.2652429334075,
      "y": 221.84295638041363,
      "width": 893.7432250976562,
      "height": 1880,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1293016566,
      "version": 2571,
      "versionNonce": 138805494,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "UFNVjqeowKNI-hptcynWf",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1746596994962,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NFR: \n- game durable \n- consistent\n- game creation and update service should be scaled. \n- do we want undo operation ?? -> else we have to maintain the each state event.\n\n\nEstimations: \n - write qps -> \n - read qps\n - read == write. -> in one move -> write to db.\n - storage\n\n\nEntity: \nGame, player, PlayerPiece, \n\n\nApi Design\n\nUI -> user create game with assign player -> player >=2\n\n1.  /api/v1/ludo/create POST\nRequest: [ listofplayers ] -> Response, GameId\n2. /api/v1/ludo/updatestate?gameId=\"\"&&status='START'\n3. /api/v1/ludo/updatepiece POST\nRequest [{ gameId, playerId, pieceId, location}, { gameId, playerId, pieceId, location}] // incase killing other piece\n4. /api/v1/lude?gameId = '' GET\nResponse: [{ GameMeta, Player: [{ player1, piecesLocation}, { player2, piecesLocation}...]}]\n5. /ws/v1/game?gameId=\"\" websocket\n\n\nSchema Design: \n\nGame\n- id\n- createdtime\n- updatedtime\n- authid\n- totalPlayers.\n- status // CREATED, STARTED, COMPLETED\n- version\n\nUser\n- id\n- name\n- email\n\nPlayer\n- id \n- userId\n- gameId\n\nPlayerPiece\n- id\n- gameId\n- playerId\n- location int // -1 -> home, \n\nGameAudit\n- gameId\n- datajson -> gatemeta , player details all with position.\n- createdTime\n- version -> increasing 1 - > 2 , 2 is latest than 1\n\nlet say version of game table is 2 \nand in audit we have 1 and 2\nwe do undo \n-> reduce version -> 2 ->.1 \n    fetch data from game audit to that version.\n    update player pice, game etc tables with that data. \n   \n\n\nplayer -> playerpiece (1:4)\ngame -> player (1:m) m>=2-4\n\n\nDatabase Access patter ? \n\n- get game\n- update player position , update game state.\n- not very concurrency issue \n- high requests\n- what about game who ended ??\n- we can go with MYSQL with index on gameId, playerId, payerpieceId\n\n\n\nHow to do undo ??\n\n\nHighLevelDesigning:\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NFR: \n- game durable \n- consistent\n- game creation and update service should be scaled. \n- do we want undo operation ?? -> else we have to maintain the each state event.\n\n\nEstimations: \n - write qps -> \n - read qps\n - read == write. -> in one move -> write to db.\n - storage\n\n\nEntity: \nGame, player, PlayerPiece, \n\n\nApi Design\n\nUI -> user create game with assign player -> player >=2\n\n1.  /api/v1/ludo/create POST\nRequest: [ listofplayers ] -> Response, GameId\n2. /api/v1/ludo/updatestate?gameId=\"\"&&status='START'\n3. /api/v1/ludo/updatepiece POST\nRequest [{ gameId, playerId, pieceId, location}, { gameId, playerId, pieceId, location}] // incase killing other piece\n4. /api/v1/lude?gameId = '' GET\nResponse: [{ GameMeta, Player: [{ player1, piecesLocation}, { player2, piecesLocation}...]}]\n5. /ws/v1/game?gameId=\"\" websocket\n\n\nSchema Design: \n\nGame\n- id\n- createdtime\n- updatedtime\n- authid\n- totalPlayers.\n- status // CREATED, STARTED, COMPLETED\n- version\n\nUser\n- id\n- name\n- email\n\nPlayer\n- id \n- userId\n- gameId\n\nPlayerPiece\n- id\n- gameId\n- playerId\n- location int // -1 -> home, \n\nGameAudit\n- gameId\n- datajson -> gatemeta , player details all with position.\n- createdTime\n- version -> increasing 1 - > 2 , 2 is latest than 1\n\nlet say version of game table is 2 \nand in audit we have 1 and 2\nwe do undo \n-> reduce version -> 2 ->.1 \n    fetch data from game audit to that version.\n    update player pice, game etc tables with that data. \n   \n\n\nplayer -> playerpiece (1:4)\ngame -> player (1:m) m>=2-4\n\n\nDatabase Access patter ? \n\n- get game\n- update player position , update game state.\n- not very concurrency issue \n- high requests\n- what about game who ended ??\n- we can go with MYSQL with index on gameId, playerId, payerpieceId\n\n\n\nHow to do undo ??\n\n\nHighLevelDesigning:\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
