    {
      "id": "xENZJplxrEYFB3Z0cKIM8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8288.904596052775,
      "y": -523.4746328026175,
      "width": 586.1434326171875,
      "height": 2220,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 971070058,
      "version": 2960,
      "versionNonce": 1203566506,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1746626959132,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design cricbuzz\n\n-  Different type of competition.  let say 2 P -> football, cricket\n-  each competition there will be today matches and past matches.\n-  for a particular competition and particular match can see details.\n\nHow deep we wanna go ? can we share detials ?? since\nit can be match -> team -> player -> ball -> wicket etc. \n\nUI\n- user -> came to website -> list of competition\n- open competition -> see list of matches.\n- open particular match.\n\n\nNFR:\n- highly available. \n- may be bit delay but highly available. \n- scalable.\n- what about durabilty ?? how past we want to keep\n\n\nEstimations:\n- Read qps \n- read peak qps\n- storage -> later on. \n\n\nEntity: \n- competition, match, team\n\nApi Design:\nNot focusing on other things like login etc.\n\n- fetch all competitions\n    - api/v1/cricbuzz/competitions POST paginated\n       Request: { pagsize, offset}\n       Response: [ pagsize, offset, competitionsList: [{..} , ..] ] \n\n- fetch the matches for a competition in chronological order \n   - api/v1/cricbuzz/matches POST paginated\n       Request: { pagsize, offset}\n       Response: [ pagsize, offset, competitionId , matchesList: [{..} , ..] ] \n\n- fetch the match summary\n    - api/v1/cricbuzz/match?competition='' && matchid=''. GET\n     Response: {matchDetail} statuscode 2xx, 4xx, 5xx.\n\n- live update of match\n    - ws://cricbuzz?match=id && competition=id\n    whenever update happend -> push to the client.\n\nx-token => auth\nreq-id => for debug\n\nheaders\n\n\nDatabase Scheme: \n\n1. Competition\n- Id\n- competitionName - /IPL\n- startedTime\n- location \n- ..metadata -> (headline)\n\n2. Match\n- id\n- competitionId\n- teamA\n- teamB\n- status -> Not started, Running, Ended\n..metadata -> json\n\n3. MatchTeam\n- matchid\n- teamid\n- teamscore\n- totalwicket\n- totalover -> double\n- totalplayerCount\n- summary\n- ..metadata -> json\n\n4. MatchPlayer\n- matchid\n- matchteamid\n- userId\n- batting score - run, balls, sixes, four, strikerate \n- bowling score - over, runs, average, wickets\n\n\nEvent:\n- matchid\n- overNo.\n- ballNo.\n- valid -> counting -> valie\n- score -> 1,2,4,6,0\n- wicket -> boolean\n- bowler\n- batsman\n\n\nDB choice: \n- We are fetch update with competitionid, matchid payerit\n- not filter on the metadata\n- also like no like concurrent write or kind of transaction. \n- dobument db -> btree -> index -> read efficient\n- flexible scheme \n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design cricbuzz\n\n-  Different type of competition.  let say 2 P -> football, cricket\n-  each competition there will be today matches and past matches.\n-  for a particular competition and particular match can see details.\n\nHow deep we wanna go ? can we share detials ?? since\nit can be match -> team -> player -> ball -> wicket etc. \n\nUI\n- user -> came to website -> list of competition\n- open competition -> see list of matches.\n- open particular match.\n\n\nNFR:\n- highly available. \n- may be bit delay but highly available. \n- scalable.\n- what about durabilty ?? how past we want to keep\n\n\nEstimations:\n- Read qps \n- read peak qps\n- storage -> later on. \n\n\nEntity: \n- competition, match, team\n\nApi Design:\nNot focusing on other things like login etc.\n\n- fetch all competitions\n    - api/v1/cricbuzz/competitions POST paginated\n       Request: { pagsize, offset}\n       Response: [ pagsize, offset, competitionsList: [{..} , ..] ] \n\n- fetch the matches for a competition in chronological order \n   - api/v1/cricbuzz/matches POST paginated\n       Request: { pagsize, offset}\n       Response: [ pagsize, offset, competitionId , matchesList: [{..} , ..] ] \n\n- fetch the match summary\n    - api/v1/cricbuzz/match?competition='' && matchid=''. GET\n     Response: {matchDetail} statuscode 2xx, 4xx, 5xx.\n\n- live update of match\n    - ws://cricbuzz?match=id && competition=id\n    whenever update happend -> push to the client.\n\nx-token => auth\nreq-id => for debug\n\nheaders\n\n\nDatabase Scheme: \n\n1. Competition\n- Id\n- competitionName - /IPL\n- startedTime\n- location \n- ..metadata -> (headline)\n\n2. Match\n- id\n- competitionId\n- teamA\n- teamB\n- status -> Not started, Running, Ended\n..metadata -> json\n\n3. MatchTeam\n- matchid\n- teamid\n- teamscore\n- totalwicket\n- totalover -> double\n- totalplayerCount\n- summary\n- ..metadata -> json\n\n4. MatchPlayer\n- matchid\n- matchteamid\n- userId\n- batting score - run, balls, sixes, four, strikerate \n- bowling score - over, runs, average, wickets\n\n\nEvent:\n- matchid\n- overNo.\n- ballNo.\n- valid -> counting -> valie\n- score -> 1,2,4,6,0\n- wicket -> boolean\n- bowler\n- batsman\n\n\nDB choice: \n- We are fetch update with competitionid, matchid payerit\n- not filter on the metadata\n- also like no like concurrent write or kind of transaction. \n- dobument db -> btree -> index -> read efficient\n- flexible scheme \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
