    {
      "id": "MFvXt52g1Bl7_yR4q47Eg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10365.524027241308,
      "y": -383.94952293052313,
      "width": 375.207763671875,
      "height": 516.9760437533896,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b99",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1905158070,
      "version": 596,
      "versionNonce": 1720249194,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1746626959132,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "url shortner\n\n1. id -> url\n\n\nqps \nstorage \ntotal ids in 5 year\nsize ? in bits -> logs2(total peak req in 5 years)\n\nglobal unique distributed id \n64 bit -> sonyflake id generator\n\n\nid url createdtime expirationtime -> dynamodb. \n\npartition key id sort key createdtime. \n\n\n/api/v1/\n\n301 -> redirect to url\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 15.906955192411989,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "url shortner\n\n1. id -> url\n\n\nqps \nstorage \ntotal ids in 5 year\nsize ? in bits -> logs2(total peak req in 5 years)\n\nglobal unique distributed id \n64 bit -> sonyflake id generator\n\n\nid url createdtime expirationtime -> dynamodb. \n\npartition key id sort key createdtime. \n\n\n/api/v1/\n\n301 -> redirect to url\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NvW0t0wKkRgnvsstsHMsb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10368.219389709859,
      "y": 232.03264840151786,
      "width": 801.1513061523438,
      "height": 1360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1835789162,
      "version": 1983,
      "versionNonce": 502001194,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1746626959132,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Splitwise lld\n\n\n1. list of group\n2. group -> people , list of expenses\n3. simplify expenses\n\n\nUI \n\n1. create group \n    -> make entry in group table, groupmember\n2. add member to group.\n    -> add entry in group memeber table.\n3. add expense.\n    -> add entry in expense table\n    -> fetch existing netbalance for the expense share person and update it and insert in groupmember\n    -> calculate simplified transaction , upsert them \n4. fetch the list of groups\n    -> fetch from group table with id\n5. fetch the expense summary of group (expenses and simplify )\n    -> fetch simplified transaction for that user\n    -> can use cache here if require.\n\ndbschem\n\ngroup\n- id\n- name\n- createdTime\n- createdBy\n- updatedTime\n- updatedBy...\n\nUser\n- id\n- email\n- name\n- phone.no\n\nGroupMember\n- id\n- groupid\n- userid\n- netbalance\n\nexpense\n- id\n- groupid\n- type // EQUAL, PERCENTAGE, EXACT\n- amount\n\nbreak expense\n\nexpenseshare\n- expenseid\n- id\n- userid\n- amount -> 5 ( type percentage )\n- estimatedamount ( 500 ) \n\n\nSimplifed transaction\n- from\n- to\n- groupid\n- amount\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Splitwise lld\n\n\n1. list of group\n2. group -> people , list of expenses\n3. simplify expenses\n\n\nUI \n\n1. create group \n    -> make entry in group table, groupmember\n2. add member to group.\n    -> add entry in group memeber table.\n3. add expense.\n    -> add entry in expense table\n    -> fetch existing netbalance for the expense share person and update it and insert in groupmember\n    -> calculate simplified transaction , upsert them \n4. fetch the list of groups\n    -> fetch from group table with id\n5. fetch the expense summary of group (expenses and simplify )\n    -> fetch simplified transaction for that user\n    -> can use cache here if require.\n\ndbschem\n\ngroup\n- id\n- name\n- createdTime\n- createdBy\n- updatedTime\n- updatedBy...\n\nUser\n- id\n- email\n- name\n- phone.no\n\nGroupMember\n- id\n- groupid\n- userid\n- netbalance\n\nexpense\n- id\n- groupid\n- type // EQUAL, PERCENTAGE, EXACT\n- amount\n\nbreak expense\n\nexpenseshare\n- expenseid\n- id\n- userid\n- amount -> 5 ( type percentage )\n- estimatedamount ( 500 ) \n\n\nSimplifed transaction\n- from\n- to\n- groupid\n- amount\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0vKmF4CAXbRK7gYRkHiDl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5129.357850269293,
      "y": 998.8293199030824,
      "width": 651.839599609375,
      "height": 620,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 439921194,
      "version": 994,
      "versionNonce": 100898922,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1746626956146,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a Parking Lot (LLD)\n\n1.  multiple storey in a building\n2.  each storey have place holder for parking. \n3.  each placeholder can be bike or car.\n4.  payment receipt, \n\n\nFlow -> user -> for parking -> search placeholder -> from bottom to up\n        -> find -> create receipt -> park \nunpark -> search storey and placeholder unpark -> check payment done or not -> if \nyes -> empty placeholder -> update status of receipt.\n\nwhat about payment ?? -> x/hour\n\n\napi design: \n\n1. parkVechile. -> receipt\n2. do payment \n3. unpark vehicle\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a Parking Lot (LLD)\n\n1.  multiple storey in a building\n2.  each storey have place holder for parking. \n3.  each placeholder can be bike or car.\n4.  payment receipt, \n\n\nFlow -> user -> for parking -> search placeholder -> from bottom to up\n        -> find -> create receipt -> park \nunpark -> search storey and placeholder unpark -> check payment done or not -> if \nyes -> empty placeholder -> update status of receipt.\n\nwhat about payment ?? -> x/hour\n\n\napi design: \n\n1. parkVechile. -> receipt\n2. do payment \n3. unpark vehicle\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DH-MtF9I6TyfPTXXmGdEm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11394.970729507879,
      "y": -439.7703845732966,
      "width": 791.9830932617188,
      "height": 820,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1248979882,
      "version": 1315,
      "versionNonce": 802006122,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1746629224700,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Distributed Rate limiter:\n\n\n- is it server level ? yes\n- at what we wannt limit ? \n    - ip \n    - overall api or how ? \n\n\n\n\nalgo\n\n1.  bucket -> increase value if greater than threshold ignore , let say 10/second, after each second \n    reset -> need to decide the threshold.\n2. sliding window -> maintain the timestamd list -> when request come remove old one and check\n    size of list. storage. \n3. normal window -> like 1:00 - 1:02 - 1:03, allow x request in 1:00-1:02 -> issue 1:01-1:03 can have > x\n\nWe can go with bucket or sliding window.\n\n\nwhat to do when scale server. \n\n\n- we can move to redis. \n- can use lua scription for making sure accuracy. \n\nwhat about durability ?  -> we can have primary and seconday replica to have high availability. \npast data we don't need, or we can have oncall or alert on rate limiting error -> rare case \nwhat about latency ? -> else it can allow the request in case of race request.\n\n\napi \n\n-> Return 429  to many request\nresponse header -> limiting, \n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Distributed Rate limiter:\n\n\n- is it server level ? yes\n- at what we wannt limit ? \n    - ip \n    - overall api or how ? \n\n\n\n\nalgo\n\n1.  bucket -> increase value if greater than threshold ignore , let say 10/second, after each second \n    reset -> need to decide the threshold.\n2. sliding window -> maintain the timestamd list -> when request come remove old one and check\n    size of list. storage. \n3. normal window -> like 1:00 - 1:02 - 1:03, allow x request in 1:00-1:02 -> issue 1:01-1:03 can have > x\n\nWe can go with bucket or sliding window.\n\n\nwhat to do when scale server. \n\n\n- we can move to redis. \n- can use lua scription for making sure accuracy. \n\nwhat about durability ?  -> we can have primary and seconday replica to have high availability. \npast data we don't need, or we can have oncall or alert on rate limiting error -> rare case \nwhat about latency ? -> else it can allow the request in case of race request.\n\n\napi \n\n-> Return 429  to many request\nresponse header -> limiting, \n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wrcXo8Eh5yYT8rD_c5Ox2",
      "type": "text",
